One Night at Egulac is a 1985 Canadian film based on the novel One Night at Egulac by Arthur Mamet. It was directed by Claude Bertrand and stars Christopher Plummer, Louis Gossett, Jr., and Anthony Quinn. The film is set in 1870s Alberta and tells the story of two rivals who spend one night at a saloon in the town of Egulac. The film was chosen by the National Film Board of Canada to represent Canada at the 1986 Cannes Film Festival.


